{"id":"CVE-2022-0391","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2022-02-09T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-14T12:12:30.872Z","description":"A flaw was found in Python, specifically within the urllib.parse module. This module helps break Uniform Resource Locator (URL) strings into components. The issue involves how the urlparse method does not sanitize input and allows characters like '\\r' and '\\n' in the URL path. This flaw allows an attacker to input a crafted URL, leading to injection attacks. This flaw affects Python versions prior to 3.10.0b1, 3.9.5, 3.8.11, 3.7.11 and 3.6.14.","cwe":["CWE-74 CWE-74"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":7.5,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"python","versions":["affected python 3.10.0b1, python 3.9.5, python 3.8.11, python 3.7.11, python 3.6.14"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.0 <V3.1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugs.python.org/issue43882"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/UDBDBAU6HUPZHISBOARTXZ5GKHF2VH5U/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-ef99a016f6"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/CSD2YBXP3ZF44E44QMIIAR5VTO35KTRB/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-18ad73aba6"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpuapr2022.html"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20220225-0009/"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202305-02","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-202305-02"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2023/09/msg00022.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20230920 [SECURITY] [DLA 3575-1] python2.7 security update"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2025/03/msg00013.html"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2024/11/msg00024.html"},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-398330.html"}],"vendors":["python"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-28696","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"intel","published":"2022-08-18T19:57:53.000Z","updated":"2025-05-05T16:21:40.833Z","description":"Uncontrolled search path in the Intel(R) Distribution for Python before version 2022.0.3 may allow an authenticated user to potentially enable escalation of privilege via local access.","cwe":["escalation of privilege","CWE-427 CWE-427 Uncontrolled Search Path Element"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":7.8,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"Intel(R) Distribution for Python","versions":["affected before version 2022.0.3"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/security-center/advisory/intel-sa-00684.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["intel","python"]}
{"id":"CVE-2022-42919","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2022-11-06T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-11-03T21:46:36.550Z","description":"Python 3.9.x before 3.9.16 and 3.10.x before 3.10.9 on Linux allows local privilege escalation in a non-default configuration. The Python multiprocessing library, when used with the forkserver start method on Linux, allows pickles to be deserialized from any user in the same machine local network namespace, which in many system configurations means any user on the same machine. Pickles can execute arbitrary code. Thus, this allows for local user privilege escalation to the user that any forkserver process is running as. Setting multiprocessing.util.abstract_sockets_supported to False is a workaround. The forkserver start method for multiprocessing is not the default start method. This issue is Linux specific because only Linux supports abstract namespace sockets. CPython before 3.9 does not make use of Linux abstract namespace sockets by default. Support for users manually specifying an abstract namespace socket was added as a bugfix in 3.7.8 and 3.8.3, but users would need to make specific uncommon API calls in order to do that in CPython before 3.9.","cwe":["n/a","CWE-502 CWE-502 Deserialization of Untrusted Data"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":7.8,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/97514"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/PI5DYIED6U26BGX5IRZWNCP6TY4M2ZGZ/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-1166a1df1e"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/VCRKBB5Y5EWTJUNC7LK665WO64DDXSTN/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-028c09eaa7"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/FKGCQPIVHEAIJ77R3RSNSQWYBUDVWDKU/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-b17bf30e88"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/P2LHWWEI5OBQ6RELULMVU6KMDYG4WZXH/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-462f39dd2f"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/XX6LLAXGZVZ327REY6MDZRMMP47LJ53P/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-a7cad6bd22"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/R6KGIRHSENZ4QAB234Z36HVIDTRJ3MFI/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2022-f44dd1bec2"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20221209-0006/"},{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/97514#issuecomment-1310277840"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/QLUGZSEAO3MBWGKCUSMKQIRYJZKJCIOB/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2023-af5206f71d"},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/RDK3ZZBRYFO47ET3N4BNTKVXN47U6ICY/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FEDORA-2023-097dd40685"},{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/compare/v3.10.8...v3.10.9"},{"url":"https://github.com/python/cpython/compare/v3.9.15...v3.9.16"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/202305-02","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-202305-02"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2024/12/msg00000.html"}],"vendors":["python"]}
